### Health check
GET http://localhost:3000/health

### Register a user
POST http://localhost:3000/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "alice",
  "password": "correct-horse-battery-staple"
}

### Login — correct password (expect 200 + token)
POST http://localhost:3000/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "alice",
  "password": "correct-horse-battery-staple"
}

### Login — wrong password (expect 401)
POST http://localhost:3000/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "alice",
  "password": "wrong-password"
}

### Benign search (expect 200)
GET http://localhost:3000/api/search/vulnerable?q=laptop

### SQLi payload against the vulnerable endpoint (still expect 200 — no
### detection middleware exists yet until Phase 3; this endpoint just
### reflects the constructed query for inspection)
GET http://localhost:3000/api/search/vulnerable?q=' OR '1'='1

### Same SQLi payload against the secure endpoint (expect 200, no match)
GET http://localhost:3000/api/search/secure?q=' OR '1'='1

### Protected resource without a token (expect 401)
GET http://localhost:3000/api/orders/123

### Protected resource with a token (replace TOKEN with a value from the
### login response above; expect 200)
GET http://localhost:3000/api/orders/123
Authorization: Bearer TOKEN
